      "content": "{\n  \"verdict\": \"MAJOR_BUG\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The function incorrectly uses min(lo, max(hi, x)). This will clamp x to [lo, hi] only if lo <= hi, but the logic is reversed: max(hi, x) returns the larger of hi and x, then min(lo, ...) returns the smaller of lo and that result \u2014 which means if x is greater than hi, max(hi, x) becomes x, and min(lo, x) will return lo if lo < x \u2014 effectively clamping to lo even if lo is less than hi. The correct logic should be min(hi, max(lo, x)) to ensure x is bounded below by lo and above by hi. This function will produce incorrect results for any x outside [lo, hi].\"\n}"
